Indeed.  You need to update libc and gcc.

I woud try running:

apt-get install build-essential

You will probably get a whole lot of warnings, including being told to run:

apt-get -f install

after that run

apt-get upgrade

That should upgrade the toolchain.  Make sure that you have libc6.1,
libc-bin, etc., at version 2.13-18, gcc-4.4 at 4.4.6-10, binutils at
2.21.53.20110823-3.

Cheers
Michael.



