For the first time in a few months I was able to run 'apt-get
dist-upgrade' on my Alpha unstable installation.

However, be aware that the new udev seems faulty.  It continually printed:

udevd[448]: unable to receive ctrl connection: Function not implemented

in my logs files, completely loaded up the CPU and filled the system
disk within 30 minutes.

Downgrading udev back to 166-1 worked for me.

Cheers
Michael.



